{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AA3rgzb9t8vijVFcCUyPf1","type":"tool_result","content":"#!/bin/sh\n# cve scanner: known vulnerabilities in dependencies, as ard findings.\n#\n# Contract (see docs/proposal.md, Scanners):\n#   - cwd is a read-only worktree of origin/main. This script finds its siblings\n#     (merge.jq, no-govulncheck) from its own path, never from cwd or /role.\n#   - Prints findings as JSON lines on stdout, and only as its very last action:\n#     any failure exits non-zero with nothing on stdout, and the controller\n#     discards the run. It never prints partial results.\n#   - Writes nothing outside a mktemp dir that is removed on exit. HOME may be\n#     unwritable. It holds no GitHub token and needs none.\n#   - stderr is the job log: tool versions, one line per Go module, final count.\n#\n# Tools (pinned in ./Dockerfile): osv-scanner v2 for every ecosystem, govulncheck\n# for Go reachability, jq for merge.jq. Exit codes: 0 success, 1 failure,\n# 2 a required tool is missing.\n#\n# Go toolchain: each module is analysed with the image's Go unless its go\n# directive (or a newer \"toolchain\" line) needs a newer one. Then scan lets Go\n# pick the version (GOTOOLCHAIN=auto rules), downloads it from the Go module\n# proxy (checksum-verified against sum.golang.org, so the job needs egress to\n# proxy.golang.org and sum.golang.org) into its temp dir, rebuilds the same\n# govulncheck version with it (about 550 MB of temp disk and 15 s per\n# toolchain, once per run), and scans with that pair. The temp dir must allow\n# exec: a noexec one fails only modules that need a switch, with a message\n# naming it. Any failure to get or build the toolchain fails the run.\n#\n# Opt-out: a human-owned file named \"no-govulncheck\" next to this script skips\n# govulncheck for repos that cannot build; reachability is then \"unknown\".\nset -eu\n\ndir=$(CDPATH= cd -- \"$(dirname -- \"$0\")\" && pwd)\n\ndie() { echo \"cve: $*\" >&2; exit 1; }\nneed() { command -v \"$1\" >/dev/null 2>&1 || { echo \"cve: $1 not found\" >&2; exit 2; }; }\n\nneed osv-scanner\nneed jq\n\n# ver_le A B: true if Go version A <= B (go1.27, go1.27.4, 1.27.0). Anything\n# that is not plain numbers (release candidates) counts as newer.\nver_le() {\n  a=${1#go} b=${2#go}\n  case $a$b in *[!0-9.]*) return 1 ;; esac\n  IFS=. read -r a1 a2 a3 <<VEREOF\n$a\nVEREOF\n  IFS=. read -r b1 b2 b3 <<VEREOF\n$b\nVEREOF\n  [ \"${a1:-0}\" -lt \"${b1:-0}\" ] && return 0\n  [ \"${a1:-0}\" -gt \"${b1:-0}\" ] && return 1\n  [ \"${a2:-0}\" -lt \"${b2:-0}\" ] && return 0\n  [ \"${a2:-0}\" -gt \"${b2:-0}\" ] && return 1\n  [ \"${a3:-0}\" -le \"${b3:-0}\" ]\n}\n\ntmp=$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/ard-cve.XXXXXX\")\n# Go's module cache is read-only on disk; make it removable first.\ncleanup() { chmod -R u+w \"$tmp\" 2>/dev/null || true; rm -rf \"$tmp\"; }\ntrap cleanup EXIT\ntrap 'exit 130' INT\ntrap 'exit 143' TERM\n\n# Keep Go's caches off an unwritable HOME and out of the worktree.\nfor v in GOCACHE GOMODCACHE GOPATH; do\n  eval \"cur=\\${$v:-}\"\n  if [ -z \"$cur\" ] || [ ! -w \"$cur\" ]; then\n    eval \"$v=\\$tmp/$v; export $v\"\n  fi\ndone\n# GOTOOLCHAIN=local: nothing may switch toolchains implicitly (host-mode go.env\n# defaults to auto). The one deliberate switch is done explicitly below.\nGOWORK=off GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly GOTOOLCHAIN=local\nexport GOWORK GOFLAGS GOTOOLCHAIN\n\necho \"osv-scanner: $(osv-scanner --version 2>&1 | head -n 1 || true)\" >&2\n\n# 1. osv-scanner. 0 = clean, 1 = vulnerabilities found, 128 = nothing to scan.\n# Its own Go call analysis is off so govulncheck is the one reachability source.\nrc=0\nosv-scanner scan source --recursive --no-call-analysis=all --format json . \\\n  > \"$tmp/osv.json\" || rc=$?\ncase $rc in\n  0|1) ;;\n  128) echo \"cve: osv-scanner found no packages\" >&2\n       echo '{\"results\":[]}' > \"$tmp/osv.json\" ;;\n  *) die \"osv-scanner failed with exit status $rc\" ;;\nesac\n\n# 2. govulncheck, once per Go module. Fail closed: a module that cannot be\n# analysed fails the run, because silently degrading would flap severity.\n: > \"$tmp/govuln.jsonl\"\nfind . \\( -name .git -o -name vendor -o -name node_modules -o -name testdata \\) -prune \\\n  -o -name go.mod -type f -print > \"$tmp/mods.raw\" || die \"find failed\"\nLC_ALL=C sort \"$tmp/mods.raw\" > \"$tmp/mods.txt\"\n\nif [ -s \"$tmp/mods.txt\" ]; then\n  if [ -e \"$dir/no-govulncheck\" ]; then\n    echo \"govulncheck: skipped (no-govulncheck present); reachability unknown\" >&2\n  else\n    need go\n    need govulncheck\n    scanner=$(govulncheck -version 2>&1 | grep -m 1 '^Scanner:' || true)\n    echo \"govulncheck: $scanner\" >&2\n    local_go=$(cd -- \"$tmp\" && go env GOVERSION) || die \"cannot run go env GOVERSION\"\n    echo \"govulncheck: image go is $local_go\" >&2\n    while IFS= read -r f; do\n      manifest=${f#./}\n      mdir=$(dirname -- \"$manifest\")\n      echo \"govulncheck: $manifest\" >&2\n      gv=govulncheck gvpath=$PATH tc= need_sw=0 why=\n      # Fast path: the image's Go can load the module. A \"toolchain\" line newer\n      # than the image's Go also needs a switch, though go list -m accepts it.\n      if ! (cd -- \"$mdir\" && go list -m) >/dev/null 2>\"$tmp/sel.err\"; then\n        need_sw=1 why=$(tail -n 1 \"$tmp/sel.err\")\n      else\n        tl=$(sed -n 's/^toolchain[[:space:]][[:space:]]*\\(go[^[:space:]]*\\).*/\\1/p' \"$manifest\" | head -n 1)\n        if [ -n \"$tl\" ] && ! ver_le \"$tl\" \"$local_go\"; then need_sw=1; fi\n      fi\n      if [ \"$need_sw\" = 1 ]; then\n        # The temp dir holds the downloaded toolchain: it must be exec-capable.\n        # Probe before any download so a noexec dir never pulls 300 MB first.\n        # The toolchain lands in GOMODCACHE: keep it in the exec-checked dir.\n        GOMODCACHE=$tmp/GOMODCACHE; export GOMODCACHE\n        printf '#!/bin/sh\\nexit 0\\n' > \"$tmp/exec-probe\" && chmod 700 \"$tmp/exec-probe\"\n        \"$tmp/exec-probe\" 2>/dev/null || die \"$manifest needs a newer Go than the image's $local_go (${why:-newer toolchain line}), but the temp dir ${TMPDIR:-/tmp} is noexec so a downloaded toolchain cannot run: set TMPDIR to an exec-capable directory or use a newer cve image\"\n        # Let Go pick the version from go.mod (go and toolchain lines).\n        sel=$(cd -- \"$mdir\" && GOTOOLCHAIN=auto go env GOVERSION 2>\"$tmp/sel.err\") \\\n          || die \"cannot get a Go toolchain for $manifest: $(tail -n 1 \"$tmp/sel.err\")\"\n        case $sel in *[!0-9a-z.]*|go|go[!0-9]*) die \"unexpected Go version for $manifest: $sel\" ;; esac\n        if [ \"$sel\" = \"$local_go\" ]; then\n          [ -z \"$why\" ] || die \"go list -m failed in $manifest: $why\"\n        else\n          groot=$(cd -- \"$tmp\" && GOTOOLCHAIN=$sel go env GOROOT 2>\"$tmp/sel.err\") \\\n            || die \"cannot get a Go toolchain for $manifest: $(tail -n 1 \"$tmp/sel.err\")\"\n          [ \"$(cd -- \"$tmp\" && \"$groot/bin/go\" env GOVERSION 2>/dev/null)\" = \"$sel\" ] \\\n            || die \"toolchain for $manifest is not $sel\"\n          gv=$tmp/gv/$sel/govulncheck gvpath=$groot/bin:$PATH tc=$sel\n          if [ ! -x \"$gv\" ]; then\n            ver=${scanner#Scanner: govulncheck@}\n            case $ver in\n              v*[!0-9.]*|v|*..*|*.|v*.) die \"unknown govulncheck version \\\"$ver\\\": cannot rebuild it with $sel\" ;;\n              v[0-9]*.[0-9]*.[0-9]*) ;;\n              *) die \"unknown govulncheck version \\\"$ver\\\": cannot rebuild it with $sel\" ;;\n            esac\n            echo \"govulncheck: building $ver with $sel for $manifest\" >&2\n            (cd -- \"$tmp\" && PATH=$gvpath CGO_ENABLED=0 GOBIN=$tmp/gv/$sel \\\n              go install \"golang.org/x/vuln/cmd/govulncheck@$ver\") >&2 \\\n              || die \"cannot build govulncheck $ver with $sel for $manifest\"\n          fi\n        fi\n      fi\n      (cd -- \"$mdir\" && PATH=$gvpath \"$gv\" -format json ./...) > \"$tmp/gv.raw\" \\\n        || die \"govulncheck failed in $manifest\"\n      jq -c -s --arg manifest \"$manifest\" --arg tc \"$tc\" \\\n        '{manifest: $manifest, messages: .} + (if $tc == \"\" then {} else {toolchain: $tc} end)' \\\n        \"$tmp/gv.raw\" >> \"$tmp/govuln.jsonl\" || die \"cannot parse govulncheck output for $manifest\"\n    done < \"$tmp/mods.txt\"\n  fi\nfi\n\n# 3. Merge into findings.\n# osv-scanner uses the logical cwd for its absolute paths; strip either form.\nroot=$(pwd -P)\nlroot=$(pwd)\njq -c -n --arg root \"$root\" --arg lroot \"$lroot\" --slurpfile osv \"$tmp/osv.json\" --slurpfile gv \"$tmp/govuln.jsonl\" \\\n  -f \"$dir/merge.jq\" > \"$tmp/out.jsonl\" || die \"merge failed\"\n\necho \"cve: $(wc -l < \"$tmp/out.jsonl\" | tr -d ' ') finding(s)\" >&2\ncat \"$tmp/out.jsonl\"\n# Pinned tool image for the cve scanner. Versions verified 2026-11-21:\n#   govulncheck v1.10.0 (golang.org/x/vuln), osv-scanner v2.7.1, jq 1.8.2.\n# The osv-scanner and jq checksums below come from the projects' own published\n# checksum files (osv-scanner_SHA256SUMS, sha256sum.txt) for those releases.\n# The base image (golang:1.27.4-trixie, git 2.47) is pinned by multi-arch index\n# digest, verified 2026-11-23 with:\n#   docker buildx imagetools inspect golang:1.27.4-trixie\n# Not bookworm: its git 2.39 breaks the committer's fetches (#163), and the ard\n# image (root Dockerfile) uses the same base.\n# Docker ignores the tag when a digest is present; it is there for readers.\n#\n# The image does NOT copy `scan` or `merge.jq`: the executor mounts this role\n# directory read-only, so the mounted script is always the one that runs.\n# Run:  docker run --rm -v \"$PWD\":/repo:ro -v <role dir>:/role:ro -w /repo IMAGE /role/scan\n\nARG GO_IMAGE=golang:1.27.4-trixie@sha256:f18c3d73a184fb0582828510722e723b63a93f7188d11dd223d9be6f6880e65d\n\nFROM ${GO_IMAGE} AS govulncheck\nARG GOVULNCHECK_VERSION=v1.10.0\nRUN CGO_ENABLED=0 GOBIN=/out go install golang.org/x/vuln/cmd/govulncheck@${GOVULNCHECK_VERSION}\n\nFROM ${GO_IMAGE} AS tools\nARG TARGETARCH\nARG OSV_SCANNER_VERSION=v2.7.1\nARG OSV_SCANNER_SHA256_AMD64=fb7dab19a8bd9bbe5c3189f09d4b7ee1820c9553a23bac202648a56efd2f6ee8\nARG OSV_SCANNER_SHA256_ARM64=983d22fbad9724514e3fcc6acc83b5fa64c5ffa6b0d9f510028f22c1b223ff81\nARG JQ_VERSION=1.8.2\nARG JQ_SHA256_AMD64=b1c22172dd303f3be49e935aa56aa48a8b7a46e0bc838b4997d3bb451495870f\nARG JQ_SHA256_ARM64=8b85c817833814ddca00a144c33705546355afccf0cf39b188f3cdb48b852309\nRUN set -eu; \\\n    case \"${TARGETARCH}\" in \\\n      amd64) osv_sha=\"${OSV_SCANNER_SHA256_AMD64}\"; jq_sha=\"${JQ_SHA256_AMD64}\" ;; \\\n      arm64) osv_sha=\"${OSV_SCANNER_SHA256_ARM64}\"; jq_sha=\"${JQ_SHA256_ARM64}\" ;; \\\n      *) echo \"unsupported arch: ${TARGETARCH}\" >&2; exit 1 ;; \\\n    esac; \\\n    mkdir /out; \\\n    curl -fsSL -o /out/osv-scanner \"https://github.com/google/osv-scanner/releases/download/${OSV_SCANNER_VERSION}/osv-scanner_linux_${TARGETARCH}\"; \\\n    echo \"${osv_sha}  /out/osv-scanner\" | sha256sum -c -; \\\n    curl -fsSL -o /out/jq \"https://github.com/jqlang/jq/releases/download/jq-${JQ_VERSION}/jq-linux-${TARGETARCH}\"; \\\n    echo \"${jq_sha}  /out/jq\" | sha256sum -c -; \\\n    chmod 0755 /out/osv-scanner /out/jq\n\n# The final image keeps the Go toolchain: govulncheck needs it to load packages.\nFROM ${GO_IMAGE}\nCOPY --from=govulncheck /out/govulncheck /usr/local/bin/govulncheck\nCOPY --from=tools /out/osv-scanner /usr/local/bin/osv-scanner\nCOPY --from=tools /out/jq /usr/local/bin/jq\n# The executor's /tmp is a noexec tmpfs, so the scan's temp dir (which holds a\n# downloaded newer Go toolchain, see scan) lives in /var/tmp: exec-capable and\n# writable by any --user. GOTOOLCHAIN=local: scan switches toolchains itself.\nENV GOTOOLCHAIN=local\nENV TMPDIR=/var/tmp\n# ard configuration, proposed by `ard init`. Edit freely; this file is yours.\n# Anything unset takes its built-in default (docs/proposal.md, Configuration).\n# Validate with `ard config check`. ard serve reads this file from origin/main.\n\n# label: only issues a maintainer labels for triage enter the pipeline.\n# all: every human-filed issue enters.\nintake: { mode: label }\n\nmerge:\n  # A PR touching any of these waits for a human approval. There is no\n  # built-in list: removing an entry removes its gate. An entry ending in /\n  # is a directory prefix; anything else is a glob (quote globs starting with *).\n  protected_paths:\n    - .github/\n    - .ard/config.yaml\n    - .ard/scanners/\n    - .ard/triage/\n    - .ard/workers/\n    - .ard/reviewers/\n    - \"**/CODEOWNERS\"\n    # Agent instructions a PR could plant to steer later agents.\n    - CLAUDE.md\n    - \"**/CLAUDE.md\"\n    - AGENTS.md\n    - \"**/AGENTS.md\"\n    - .claude/\n    - .mcp.json\n\noverrides:\n  scanners/cve: { every: 6h, max_open: 10, group_size: 1, autoclose: true }\n  triage/lead:  { model: claude-opus-5-5, timeout: 15m }\n  triage/engineer: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5 }\n  # timeout covers the whole worker job (agent, tests, fix rounds). tests is your\n  # repo's test command; \"\" turns the test step off.\n  workers/engineer: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5, timeout: 60m, tests: make test }\n  reviewers/eng-review: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5 }\n// Package roles holds the starter .ard/ tree that `ard init` (#27) proposes\n// to a target repo. Paths in FS are relative to .ard/ (for example\n// \"config.yaml\" or \"scanners/cve/scan\"). embed.FS reports every file as 0444,\n// so the writer must commit files named in ExecutableNames as 100755.\npackage roles\n\nimport \"embed\"\n\n// FS is the starter .ard/ tree `ard init` proposes: config.yaml plus the role\n// directories (scanners/cve, triage/lead, triage/engineer, workers/engineer and reviewers/eng-review); paths are relative to .ard/.\n//\n//go:embed config.yaml reviewers scanners triage workers\nvar FS embed.FS\n\n// ExecutableNames lists base names that must be written 0755.\nvar ExecutableNames = []string{\"scan\"}\nscanners/cve:\nDockerfile\nmerge.jq\nscan\n\ntestdata:\ncve\npackage scanner\n\nimport (\n\t\"bufio\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"io\"\n\t\"path\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"unicode\"\n\t\"unicode/utf8\"\n)\n\n// Severity of a finding.\ntype Severity string\n\n// The five severities, highest first.\nconst (\n\tSevCritical Severity = \"critical\"\n\tSevHigh     Severity = \"high\"\n\tSevMedium   Severity = \"medium\"\n\tSevLow      Severity = \"low\"\n\tSevInfo     Severity = \"info\"\n)\n\n// Rank orders severities: critical is 5, info is 1, an unknown value is 0.\nfunc (s Severity) Rank() int {\n\tswitch s {\n\tcase SevCritical:\n\t\treturn 5\n\tcase SevHigh:\n\t\treturn 4\n\tcase SevMedium:\n\t\treturn 3\n\tcase SevLow:\n\t\treturn 2\n\tcase SevInfo:\n\t\treturn 1\n\t}\n\treturn 0\n}\n\n// Valid reports whether s is one of the five severities.\nfunc (s Severity) Valid() bool { return s.Rank() > 0 }\n\n// Limits on scanner output. Any violation fails the whole run.\nconst (\n\tMaxLineBytes   = 1 << 20  // one JSONL line\n\tMaxStreamBytes = 16 << 20 // the whole stdout\n\tMaxFindings    = 10000\n\tMaxBodyBytes   = 64 << 10\n\tMaxFingerprint = 512 // bytes\n\tMaxTitleRunes  = 200\n\tMaxGroupBytes  = 256\n\tMaxFiles       = 1000\n\tmaxPathBytes   = 4096\n\tmaxErrorLines  = 20\n)\n\n// Finding is one line of scanner output.\ntype Finding struct {\n\tFingerprint string   `json:\"fingerprint\"` // required; stable across runs\n\tTitle       string   `json:\"title\"`       // required; one line\n\tSeverity    Severity `json:\"severity\"`    // required\n\tGroup       string   `json:\"group\"`       // optional; \"\" = one issue per finding\n\tFiles       []string `json:\"files\"`       // optional; repo-relative\n\tBody        string   `json:\"body\"`        // optional markdown\n}\n\n// DecodeError is one invalid line of scanner output.\ntype DecodeError struct {\n\tLine int\n\tMsg  string\n}\n\nfunc (e DecodeError) Error() string { return fmt.Sprintf(\"line %d: %s\", e.Line, e.Msg) }\n\n// DecodeErrors lists the invalid lines of a scanner's output, at most 20.\ntype DecodeErrors []DecodeError\n\nfunc (e DecodeErrors) Error() string {\nroles_test.go:32:\twant := []string{\"config.yaml\", \"reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\", \"scanners/cve/Dockerfile\", \"scanners/cve/merge.jq\", \"scanners/cve/scan\", \"triage/engineer/prompt.txt\", \"triage/lead/prompt.txt\", \"workers/engineer/prompt.txt\"}\nroles_test.go:46:\tfi, err := os.Stat(\"scanners/cve/scan\")\nroles_test.go:51:\t\tt.Fatalf(\"scanners/cve/scan mode %v has no exec bit\", fi.Mode())\nroles_test.go:75:\t\tif res.Roles[i].Kind == config.KindScanner && res.Roles[i].Name == \"cve\" {\nroles_test.go:80:\t\tt.Fatalf(\"no scanner role cve in %+v\", res.Roles)\nroles_test.go:82:\tif found.ScanPath != \".ard/scanners/cve/scan\" || found.PromptPath != \"\" || !found.Autoclose {\nroles_test.go:86:\t\tt.Errorf(\"cve overrides: every=%v max_open=%d group_size=%d, want 6h, 10, 1\", found.Every, found.MaxOpen, found.GroupSize)\nroles_test.go:88:\tif found.Dockerfile != \".ard/scanners/cve/Dockerfile\" {\n../initcmd/initcmd_test.go:145:var starterTree = []string{\".ard/config.yaml\", \".ard/reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\", \".ard/scanners/cve/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/cve/merge.jq\", \".ard/scanners/cve/scan\", \".ard/triage/engineer/prompt.txt\", \".ard/triage/lead/prompt.txt\", \".ard/workers/engineer/prompt.txt\"}\n../initcmd/initcmd_test.go:157:\tif got := strings.TrimSpace(gittest.Run(t, h.bare, \"ls-tree\", \"-r\", \"ard-init\", \"--\", \".ard/scanners/cve/scan\")); !strings.HasPrefix(got, \"100755 \") {\n../initcmd/initcmd_test.go:180:\tcve, _ := cres.Role(config.KindScanner, \"cve\")\n../initcmd/initcmd_test.go:181:\tif cve.Every != 6*time.Hour || cve.MaxOpen != 10 || cve.GroupSize != 1 || !cve.Autoclose {\n../initcmd/initcmd_test.go:182:\t\tt.Errorf(\"cve = %+v\", cve)\n../initcmd/initcmd_test.go:193:\tfor _, s := range []string{\"bot-commits.yml\", \"ARD_BOT_LOGIN\", \"Squash and merge\", \".ard/scanners/cve/scan\", \".ard/triage/lead/prompt.txt\", \".ard/triage/engineer/prompt.txt\", \".ard/workers/engineer/prompt.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\"} {\n../initcmd/initcmd_test.go:207:\t\tfound = found || l.Name == labels.Scanner(\"cve\")\n../initcmd/initcmd_test.go:210:\t\tt.Errorf(\"label %s missing: %v\", labels.Scanner(\"cve\"), have)\n../initcmd/initcmd_test.go:224:\tfor _, s := range []string{\"add  .ard/scanners/cve/scan (0755)\", \"add  .ard/config.yaml\", \"opened PR #\"} {\n../initcmd/initcmd_test.go:316:\t\t\".ard/scanners/cve/merge.jq\":    \"# identical-path, different content\\n\",\n../initcmd/initcmd_test.go:322:\t\tif err == nil || !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \".ard/config.yaml\") || !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \".ard/scanners/cve/merge.jq\") || !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"--force\") {\n../initcmd/initcmd_test.go:340:\t\tfor _, want := range []string{\".ard/12/issue.md\", \".ard/triage/custom/prompt.txt\", \".ard/config.yaml\", \".ard/scanners/cve/scan\"} {\n../initcmd/initcmd_test.go:552:\texisting[\".ard/scanners/cve/scan\"].Mode = 0o644\n../initcmd/initcmd_test.go:553:\tif _, err := plan(existing, files, false); err == nil || !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"scanners/cve/scan\") {\n../initcmd/initcmd_test.go:561:\t\tif (op.Act == actOverwrite) != (op.File.Path == \".ard/scanners/cve/scan\") {\n     982 cve_test.go\n     152 cve_docker_integration_test.go\n    1134 total","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7509fb23-cc48-478a-86a3-3a969af8b5b2","uuid":"edd3525b-aa30-42d8-900e-2c398394fa15","timestamp":"2026-11-23T15:59:40.897Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"#!/bin/sh\n# cve scanner: known vulnerabilities in dependencies, as ard findings.\n#\n# Contract (see docs/proposal.md, Scanners):\n#   - cwd is a read-only worktree of origin/main. This script finds its siblings\n#     (merge.jq, no-govulncheck) from its own path, never from cwd or /role.\n#   - Prints findings as JSON lines on stdout, and only as its very last action:\n#     any failure exits non-zero with nothing on stdout, and the controller\n#     discards the run. It never prints partial results.\n#   - Writes nothing outside a mktemp dir that is removed on exit. HOME may be\n#     unwritable. It holds no GitHub token and needs none.\n#   - stderr is the job log: tool versions, one line per Go module, final count.\n#\n# Tools (pinned in ./Dockerfile): osv-scanner v2 for every ecosystem, govulncheck\n# for Go reachability, jq for merge.jq. Exit codes: 0 success, 1 failure,\n# 2 a required tool is missing.\n#\n# Go toolchain: each module is analysed with the image's Go unless its go\n# directive (or a newer \"toolchain\" line) needs a newer one. Then scan lets Go\n# pick the version (GOTOOLCHAIN=auto rules), downloads it from the Go module\n# proxy (checksum-verified against sum.golang.org, so the job needs egress to\n# proxy.golang.org and sum.golang.org) into its temp dir, rebuilds the same\n# govulncheck version with it (about 550 MB of temp disk and 15 s per\n# toolchain, once per run), and scans with that pair. The temp dir must allow\n# exec: a noexec one fails only modules that need a switch, with a message\n# naming it. Any failure to get or build the toolchain fails the run.\n#\n# Opt-out: a human-owned file named \"no-govulncheck\" next to this script skips\n# govulncheck for repos that cannot build; reachability is then \"unknown\".\nset -eu\n\ndir=$(CDPATH= cd -- \"$(dirname -- \"$0\")\" && pwd)\n\ndie() { echo \"cve: $*\" >&2; exit 1; }\nneed() { command -v \"$1\" >/dev/null 2>&1 || { echo \"cve: $1 not found\" >&2; exit 2; }; }\n\nneed osv-scanner\nneed jq\n\n# ver_le A B: true if Go version A <= B (go1.27, go1.27.4, 1.27.0). Anything\n# that is not plain numbers (release candidates) counts as newer.\nver_le() {\n  a=${1#go} b=${2#go}\n  case $a$b in *[!0-9.]*) return 1 ;; esac\n  IFS=. read -r a1 a2 a3 <<VEREOF\n$a\nVEREOF\n  IFS=. read -r b1 b2 b3 <<VEREOF\n$b\nVEREOF\n  [ \"${a1:-0}\" -lt \"${b1:-0}\" ] && return 0\n  [ \"${a1:-0}\" -gt \"${b1:-0}\" ] && return 1\n  [ \"${a2:-0}\" -lt \"${b2:-0}\" ] && return 0\n  [ \"${a2:-0}\" -gt \"${b2:-0}\" ] && return 1\n  [ \"${a3:-0}\" -le \"${b3:-0}\" ]\n}\n\ntmp=$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/ard-cve.XXXXXX\")\n# Go's module cache is read-only on disk; make it removable first.\ncleanup() { chmod -R u+w \"$tmp\" 2>/dev/null || true; rm -rf \"$tmp\"; }\ntrap cleanup EXIT\ntrap 'exit 130' INT\ntrap 'exit 143' TERM\n\n# Keep Go's caches off an unwritable HOME and out of the worktree.\nfor v in GOCACHE GOMODCACHE GOPATH; do\n  eval \"cur=\\${$v:-}\"\n  if [ -z \"$cur\" ] || [ ! -w \"$cur\" ]; then\n    eval \"$v=\\$tmp/$v; export $v\"\n  fi\ndone\n# GOTOOLCHAIN=local: nothing may switch toolchains implicitly (host-mode go.env\n# defaults to auto). The one deliberate switch is done explicitly below.\nGOWORK=off GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly GOTOOLCHAIN=local\nexport GOWORK GOFLAGS GOTOOLCHAIN\n\necho \"osv-scanner: $(osv-scanner --version 2>&1 | head -n 1 || true)\" >&2\n\n# 1. osv-scanner. 0 = clean, 1 = vulnerabilities found, 128 = nothing to scan.\n# Its own Go call analysis is off so govulncheck is the one reachability source.\nrc=0\nosv-scanner scan source --recursive --no-call-analysis=all --format json . \\\n  > \"$tmp/osv.json\" || rc=$?\ncase $rc in\n  0|1) ;;\n  128) echo \"cve: osv-scanner found no packages\" >&2\n       echo '{\"results\":[]}' > \"$tmp/osv.json\" ;;\n  *) die \"osv-scanner failed with exit status $rc\" ;;\nesac\n\n# 2. govulncheck, once per Go module. Fail closed: a module that cannot be\n# analysed fails the run, because silently degrading would flap severity.\n: > \"$tmp/govuln.jsonl\"\nfind . \\( -name .git -o -name vendor -o -name node_modules -o -name testdata \\) -prune \\\n  -o -name go.mod -type f -print > \"$tmp/mods.raw\" || die \"find failed\"\nLC_ALL=C sort \"$tmp/mods.raw\" > \"$tmp/mods.txt\"\n\nif [ -s \"$tmp/mods.txt\" ]; then\n  if [ -e \"$dir/no-govulncheck\" ]; then\n    echo \"govulncheck: skipped (no-govulncheck present); reachability unknown\" >&2\n  else\n    need go\n    need govulncheck\n    scanner=$(govulncheck -version 2>&1 | grep -m 1 '^Scanner:' || true)\n    echo \"govulncheck: $scanner\" >&2\n    local_go=$(cd -- \"$tmp\" && go env GOVERSION) || die \"cannot run go env GOVERSION\"\n    echo \"govulncheck: image go is $local_go\" >&2\n    while IFS= read -r f; do\n      manifest=${f#./}\n      mdir=$(dirname -- \"$manifest\")\n      echo \"govulncheck: $manifest\" >&2\n      gv=govulncheck gvpath=$PATH tc= need_sw=0 why=\n      # Fast path: the image's Go can load the module. A \"toolchain\" line newer\n      # than the image's Go also needs a switch, though go list -m accepts it.\n      if ! (cd -- \"$mdir\" && go list -m) >/dev/null 2>\"$tmp/sel.err\"; then\n        need_sw=1 why=$(tail -n 1 \"$tmp/sel.err\")\n      else\n        tl=$(sed -n 's/^toolchain[[:space:]][[:space:]]*\\(go[^[:space:]]*\\).*/\\1/p' \"$manifest\" | head -n 1)\n        if [ -n \"$tl\" ] && ! ver_le \"$tl\" \"$local_go\"; then need_sw=1; fi\n      fi\n      if [ \"$need_sw\" = 1 ]; then\n        # The temp dir holds the downloaded toolchain: it must be exec-capable.\n        # Probe before any download so a noexec dir never pulls 300 MB first.\n        # The toolchain lands in GOMODCACHE: keep it in the exec-checked dir.\n        GOMODCACHE=$tmp/GOMODCACHE; export GOMODCACHE\n        printf '#!/bin/sh\\nexit 0\\n' > \"$tmp/exec-probe\" && chmod 700 \"$tmp/exec-probe\"\n        \"$tmp/exec-probe\" 2>/dev/null || die \"$manifest needs a newer Go than the image's $local_go (${why:-newer toolchain line}), but the temp dir ${TMPDIR:-/tmp} is noexec so a downloaded toolchain cannot run: set TMPDIR to an exec-capable directory or use a newer cve image\"\n        # Let Go pick the version from go.mod (go and toolchain lines).\n        sel=$(cd -- \"$mdir\" && GOTOOLCHAIN=auto go env GOVERSION 2>\"$tmp/sel.err\") \\\n          || die \"cannot get a Go toolchain for $manifest: $(tail -n 1 \"$tmp/sel.err\")\"\n        case $sel in *[!0-9a-z.]*|go|go[!0-9]*) die \"unexpected Go version for $manifest: $sel\" ;; esac\n        if [ \"$sel\" = \"$local_go\" ]; then\n          [ -z \"$why\" ] || die \"go list -m failed in $manifest: $why\"\n        else\n          groot=$(cd -- \"$tmp\" && GOTOOLCHAIN=$sel go env GOROOT 2>\"$tmp/sel.err\") \\\n            || die \"cannot get a Go toolchain for $manifest: $(tail -n 1 \"$tmp/sel.err\")\"\n          [ \"$(cd -- \"$tmp\" && \"$groot/bin/go\" env GOVERSION 2>/dev/null)\" = \"$sel\" ] \\\n            || die \"toolchain for $manifest is not $sel\"\n          gv=$tmp/gv/$sel/govulncheck gvpath=$groot/bin:$PATH tc=$sel\n          if [ ! -x \"$gv\" ]; then\n            ver=${scanner#Scanner: govulncheck@}\n            case $ver in\n              v*[!0-9.]*|v|*..*|*.|v*.) die \"unknown govulncheck version \\\"$ver\\\": cannot rebuild it with $sel\" ;;\n              v[0-9]*.[0-9]*.[0-9]*) ;;\n              *) die \"unknown govulncheck version \\\"$ver\\\": cannot rebuild it with $sel\" ;;\n            esac\n            echo \"govulncheck: building $ver with $sel for $manifest\" >&2\n            (cd -- \"$tmp\" && PATH=$gvpath CGO_ENABLED=0 GOBIN=$tmp/gv/$sel \\\n              go install \"golang.org/x/vuln/cmd/govulncheck@$ver\") >&2 \\\n              || die \"cannot build govulncheck $ver with $sel for $manifest\"\n          fi\n        fi\n      fi\n      (cd -- \"$mdir\" && PATH=$gvpath \"$gv\" -format json ./...) > \"$tmp/gv.raw\" \\\n        || die \"govulncheck failed in $manifest\"\n      jq -c -s --arg manifest \"$manifest\" --arg tc \"$tc\" \\\n        '{manifest: $manifest, messages: .} + (if $tc == \"\" then {} else {toolchain: $tc} end)' \\\n        \"$tmp/gv.raw\" >> \"$tmp/govuln.jsonl\" || die \"cannot parse govulncheck output for $manifest\"\n    done < \"$tmp/mods.txt\"\n  fi\nfi\n\n# 3. Merge into findings.\n# osv-scanner uses the logical cwd for its absolute paths; strip either form.\nroot=$(pwd -P)\nlroot=$(pwd)\njq -c -n --arg root \"$root\" --arg lroot \"$lroot\" --slurpfile osv \"$tmp/osv.json\" --slurpfile gv \"$tmp/govuln.jsonl\" \\\n  -f \"$dir/merge.jq\" > \"$tmp/out.jsonl\" || die \"merge failed\"\n\necho \"cve: $(wc -l < \"$tmp/out.jsonl\" | tr -d ' ') finding(s)\" >&2\ncat \"$tmp/out.jsonl\"\n# Pinned tool image for the cve scanner. Versions verified 2026-11-21:\n#   govulncheck v1.10.0 (golang.org/x/vuln), osv-scanner v2.7.1, jq 1.8.2.\n# The osv-scanner and jq checksums below come from the projects' own published\n# checksum files (osv-scanner_SHA256SUMS, sha256sum.txt) for those releases.\n# The base image (golang:1.27.4-trixie, git 2.47) is pinned by multi-arch index\n# digest, verified 2026-11-23 with:\n#   docker buildx imagetools inspect golang:1.27.4-trixie\n# Not bookworm: its git 2.39 breaks the committer's fetches (#163), and the ard\n# image (root Dockerfile) uses the same base.\n# Docker ignores the tag when a digest is present; it is there for readers.\n#\n# The image does NOT copy `scan` or `merge.jq`: the executor mounts this role\n# directory read-only, so the mounted script is always the one that runs.\n# Run:  docker run --rm -v \"$PWD\":/repo:ro -v <role dir>:/role:ro -w /repo IMAGE /role/scan\n\nARG GO_IMAGE=golang:1.27.4-trixie@sha256:f18c3d73a184fb0582828510722e723b63a93f7188d11dd223d9be6f6880e65d\n\nFROM ${GO_IMAGE} AS govulncheck\nARG GOVULNCHECK_VERSION=v1.10.0\nRUN CGO_ENABLED=0 GOBIN=/out go install golang.org/x/vuln/cmd/govulncheck@${GOVULNCHECK_VERSION}\n\nFROM ${GO_IMAGE} AS tools\nARG TARGETARCH\nARG OSV_SCANNER_VERSION=v2.7.1\nARG OSV_SCANNER_SHA256_AMD64=fb7dab19a8bd9bbe5c3189f09d4b7ee1820c9553a23bac202648a56efd2f6ee8\nARG OSV_SCANNER_SHA256_ARM64=983d22fbad9724514e3fcc6acc83b5fa64c5ffa6b0d9f510028f22c1b223ff81\nARG JQ_VERSION=1.8.2\nARG JQ_SHA256_AMD64=b1c22172dd303f3be49e935aa56aa48a8b7a46e0bc838b4997d3bb451495870f\nARG JQ_SHA256_ARM64=8b85c817833814ddca00a144c33705546355afccf0cf39b188f3cdb48b852309\nRUN set -eu; \\\n    case \"${TARGETARCH}\" in \\\n      amd64) osv_sha=\"${OSV_SCANNER_SHA256_AMD64}\"; jq_sha=\"${JQ_SHA256_AMD64}\" ;; \\\n      arm64) osv_sha=\"${OSV_SCANNER_SHA256_ARM64}\"; jq_sha=\"${JQ_SHA256_ARM64}\" ;; \\\n      *) echo \"unsupported arch: ${TARGETARCH}\" >&2; exit 1 ;; \\\n    esac; \\\n    mkdir /out; \\\n    curl -fsSL -o /out/osv-scanner \"https://github.com/google/osv-scanner/releases/download/${OSV_SCANNER_VERSION}/osv-scanner_linux_${TARGETARCH}\"; \\\n    echo \"${osv_sha}  /out/osv-scanner\" | sha256sum -c -; \\\n    curl -fsSL -o /out/jq \"https://github.com/jqlang/jq/releases/download/jq-${JQ_VERSION}/jq-linux-${TARGETARCH}\"; \\\n    echo \"${jq_sha}  /out/jq\" | sha256sum -c -; \\\n    chmod 0755 /out/osv-scanner /out/jq\n\n# The final image keeps the Go toolchain: govulncheck needs it to load packages.\nFROM ${GO_IMAGE}\nCOPY --from=govulncheck /out/govulncheck /usr/local/bin/govulncheck\nCOPY --from=tools /out/osv-scanner /usr/local/bin/osv-scanner\nCOPY --from=tools /out/jq /usr/local/bin/jq\n# The executor's /tmp is a noexec tmpfs, so the scan's temp dir (which holds a\n# downloaded newer Go toolchain, see scan) lives in /var/tmp: exec-capable and\n# writable by any --user. GOTOOLCHAIN=local: scan switches toolchains itself.\nENV GOTOOLCHAIN=local\nENV TMPDIR=/var/tmp\n# ard configuration, proposed by `ard init`. Edit freely; this file is yours.\n# Anything unset takes its built-in default (docs/proposal.md, Configuration).\n# Validate with `ard config check`. ard serve reads this file from origin/main.\n\n# label: only issues a maintainer labels for triage enter the pipeline.\n# all: every human-filed issue enters.\nintake: { mode: label }\n\nmerge:\n  # A PR touching any of these waits for a human approval. There is no\n  # built-in list: removing an entry removes its gate. An entry ending in /\n  # is a directory prefix; anything else is a glob (quote globs starting with *).\n  protected_paths:\n    - .github/\n    - .ard/config.yaml\n    - .ard/scanners/\n    - .ard/triage/\n    - .ard/workers/\n    - .ard/reviewers/\n    - \"**/CODEOWNERS\"\n    # Agent instructions a PR could plant to steer later agents.\n    - CLAUDE.md\n    - \"**/CLAUDE.md\"\n    - AGENTS.md\n    - \"**/AGENTS.md\"\n    - .claude/\n    - .mcp.json\n\noverrides:\n  scanners/cve: { every: 6h, max_open: 10, group_size: 1, autoclose: true }\n  triage/lead:  { model: claude-opus-5-5, timeout: 15m }\n  triage/engineer: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5 }\n  # timeout covers the whole worker job (agent, tests, fix rounds). tests is your\n  # repo's test command; \"\" turns the test step off.\n  workers/engineer: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5, timeout: 60m, tests: make test }\n  reviewers/eng-review: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5 }\n// Package roles holds the starter .ard/ tree that `ard init` (#27) proposes\n// to a target repo. Paths in FS are relative to .ard/ (for example\n// \"config.yaml\" or \"scanners/cve/scan\"). embed.FS reports every file as 0444,\n// so the writer must commit files named in ExecutableNames as 100755.\npackage roles\n\nimport \"embed\"\n\n// FS is the starter .ard/ tree `ard init` proposes: config.yaml plus the role\n// directories (scanners/cve, triage/lead, triage/engineer, workers/engineer and reviewers/eng-review); paths are relative to .ard/.\n//\n//go:embed config.yaml reviewers scanners triage workers\nvar FS embed.FS\n\n// ExecutableNames lists base names that must be written 0755.\nvar ExecutableNames = []string{\"scan\"}\nscanners/cve:\nDockerfile\nmerge.jq\nscan\n\ntestdata:\ncve\npackage scanner\n\nimport (\n\t\"bufio\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"io\"\n\t\"path\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"unicode\"\n\t\"unicode/utf8\"\n)\n\n// Severity of a finding.\ntype Severity string\n\n// The five severities, highest first.\nconst (\n\tSevCritical Severity = \"critical\"\n\tSevHigh     Severity = \"high\"\n\tSevMedium   Severity = \"medium\"\n\tSevLow      Severity = \"low\"\n\tSevInfo     Severity = \"info\"\n)\n\n// Rank orders severities: critical is 5, info is 1, an unknown value is 0.\nfunc (s Severity) Rank() int {\n\tswitch s {\n\tcase SevCritical:\n\t\treturn 5\n\tcase SevHigh:\n\t\treturn 4\n\tcase SevMedium:\n\t\treturn 3\n\tcase SevLow:\n\t\treturn 2\n\tcase SevInfo:\n\t\treturn 1\n\t}\n\treturn 0\n}\n\n// Valid reports whether s is one of the five severities.\nfunc (s Severity) Valid() bool { return s.Rank() > 0 }\n\n// Limits on scanner output. Any violation fails the whole run.\nconst (\n\tMaxLineBytes   = 1 << 20  // one JSONL line\n\tMaxStreamBytes = 16 << 20 // the whole stdout\n\tMaxFindings    = 10000\n\tMaxBodyBytes   = 64 << 10\n\tMaxFingerprint = 512 // bytes\n\tMaxTitleRunes  = 200\n\tMaxGroupBytes  = 256\n\tMaxFiles       = 1000\n\tmaxPathBytes   = 4096\n\tmaxErrorLines  = 20\n)\n\n// Finding is one line of scanner output.\ntype Finding struct {\n\tFingerprint string   `json:\"fingerprint\"` // required; stable across runs\n\tTitle       string   `json:\"title\"`       // required; one line\n\tSeverity    Severity `json:\"severity\"`    // required\n\tGroup       string   `json:\"group\"`       // optional; \"\" = one issue per finding\n\tFiles       []string `json:\"files\"`       // optional; repo-relative\n\tBody        string   `json:\"body\"`        // optional markdown\n}\n\n// DecodeError is one invalid line of scanner output.\ntype DecodeError struct {\n\tLine int\n\tMsg  string\n}\n\nfunc (e DecodeError) Error() string { return fmt.Sprintf(\"line %d: %s\", e.Line, e.Msg) }\n\n// DecodeErrors lists the invalid lines of a scanner's output, at most 20.\ntype DecodeErrors []DecodeError\n\nfunc (e DecodeErrors) Error() string {\nroles_test.go:32:\twant := []string{\"config.yaml\", \"reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\", \"scanners/cve/Dockerfile\", \"scanners/cve/merge.jq\", \"scanners/cve/scan\", \"triage/engineer/prompt.txt\", \"triage/lead/prompt.txt\", \"workers/engineer/prompt.txt\"}\nroles_test.go