{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChL9DasMT6fvcJXFsQtKH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KfRfiyqaJEiat5LkMnnoVg","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /work; grep -o \"the cve, lead[^.]*\\.\\|the cve, [a-z, ]*overrides\" docs/proposal.md | head; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='docs/proposal.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"| docs | undocumented public APIs (deterministic) plus doc drift (LLM) | 3 d | 10 | deterministic part only |\",\n\"| docs | undocumented exported Go identifiers and package comments (deterministic) | 3 d | 10 per package | yes |\\n| docs-drift | LLM: docs that contradict the code (PR B, needs the LLM scanner engine) | 3 d | 10 per doc file | no |\")\npara=\"\"\"**The docs scanner** (`scanners/docs`, a `sh` script plus one stdlib-only Go program, `docscan.go`, built at scan time with the job's own Go) lists undocumented exported Go identifiers. It reports, per package directory: a missing package comment; an exported function, a method on an exported receiver type (pointer, value or generic) and an exported type with no doc comment (the spec's doc, its trailing comment or the enclosing declaration's doc all count); and an exported const or var with no comment, one finding per parenthesised block that has no block comment. Struct fields, interface methods, methods on unexported types and comment wording are not checked. Every exported identifier counts, `internal/` included, and files for every platform count (build constraints are not evaluated). It skips `testdata/`, `vendor/`, `node_modules/` and dot or underscore directories, symlinks, `*_test.go`, `//go:build ignore` files, generated files and `package main`. The fingerprint is `docs:undoc:<dir>:<symbol>` or `docs:pkg:<dir>`; the file and line are left out, so moving a declaration within its package keeps its issue. Severity is `low` and the group is the package directory. It only parses files: it never runs repository code and needs no network. It fails closed: a parse error, unreadable file, invalid path or more than 10,000 findings fails the run with nothing filed. A human-owned `exclude` file in the role directory skips package directories (`dir/` is a directory and everything below it, anything else a glob matched against the package directory); an entry makes its findings vanish, so autoclose closes their issues. Go only for now.\n\n\"\"\"\ni=s.index(\"**The cve scanner**\")\nj=s.index(\"\\n\\n\",i)+2\ns=s[:j]+para+s[j:]\ns=s.replace(\"  scanners/cve:             { every: 6h, max_open: 10, group_size: 1, autoclose: true }\\n\",\"  scanners/cve:             { every: 6h, max_open: 10, group_size: 1, autoclose: true }\\n  scanners/docs:            { every: 3d, max_open: 3, group_size: 10, autoclose: true }\\n\",1)\ns=s.replace(\"(today `scanners/cve`, `triage/lead`\",\"(today `scanners/cve`, `scanners/docs`, `triage/lead`\",1)\ns=s.replace(\"and the cve, lead, engineer\",\"and the cve, docs, lead, engineer\",1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nc='CLAUDE.md'\nt=open(c).read()\nt=t.replace(\"(scanners/cve, triage/lead\",\"(scanners/cve, scanners/docs, triage/lead\",1)\nopen(c,'w').write(t)\nEOF\ngit diff --stat; grep -c \"cve, docs, lead\" docs/proposal.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2068,"cache_read_input_tokens":71838,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2068},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7509fb23-cc48-478a-86a3-3a969af8b5b2","uuid":"7f037351-0026-4253-8890-c8e57ceeeb99","timestamp":"2026-11-23T16:03:32.039Z","request_id":"req_011ChL9Daiw6auK6myXxcnHD"}
